{"id":"ha-giang-loop","title":"Ha Giang Loop","who":"Classic route · northern Vietnam by motorbike","when":"Best October–November (buckwheat flowers) and March–May","vehicle":"Motorbike or with an easy rider, 3–4 days","kind":"moto","color":"#c2410c","summary":"A loop of 350–450 km through the karst mountains on the Chinese border: the Ma Pi Leng pass above the Nho Que river, Hmong villages and markets, terraced valleys and homestays. Most go anticlockwise from Ha Giang; many ride pillion with a local driver.","sources":[{"label":"Kreier: the Ha Giang Loop a second time (2025)","url":"https://kreier.github.io/quartz/Travel/2025/Ha-Giang-loop-a-second-time-in-2025"},{"label":"Team-BHP travelogue: Ha Giang Loop (May 2025)","url":"https://www.team-bhp.com/forum/travelogues/294466-ha-giang-loop-vietnam.html"}],"approximate":"The usual anticlockwise loop and overnight villages.","km":448,"bbox":[104.929,22.7315,105.5482,23.3625],"stops":[{"name":"Ha Giang","place":"Ha Giang, Vietnam","at":[22.8168,104.9505],"text":"Bikes rented, permits checked, and north into the mountains.","source":{"label":"Kreier (2025)","url":"https://kreier.github.io/quartz/Travel/2025/Ha-Giang-loop-a-second-time-in-2025"}},{"name":"Heaven's Gate","place":"Quan Ba, Ha Giang","at":[23.07,104.99],"text":"The first pass, looking over the twin \"fairy\" hills of Quan Ba.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Thitrantamson.jpg/500px-Thitrantamson.jpg","page":"Quản Bạ district","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thitrantamson.jpg","credit":"Thái Nhi at vi.wikipedia","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Yen Minh","place":"Yen Minh, Ha Giang","at":[23.1172,105.1491],"text":"Pine forests and switchbacks to a small market town.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Autumn_comes_on_TerraceField-YenMinh_HaGiang_Vietnam.jpg/500px-Autumn_comes_on_TerraceField-YenMinh_HaGiang_Vietnam.jpg","page":"Yên Minh district","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Autumn_comes_on_TerraceField-YenMinh_HaGiang_Vietnam.jpg","credit":"The original uploader was BacLuong at Vietnamese Wikipedia.","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Hmong King's Palace","place":"Sa Phin, Dong Van","at":[23.2562,105.2621],"text":"The palace of the Vuong family, the old Hmong rulers of the opium trade."},{"name":"Lung Cu","place":"Lung Cu, Ha Giang","at":[23.3635,105.3163],"text":"A flag tower at Vietnam's northern tip, a detour from Dong Van."},{"name":"Dong Van","place":"Dong Van, Ha Giang","at":[23.2783,105.3622],"text":"An old town on a UNESCO geopark of karst; its Sunday market fills with people from the hill villages."},{"name":"Ma Pi Leng Pass","place":"Ma Pi Leng Pass","at":[23.2333,105.4117],"text":"The road cut into the cliffs above the Nho Que river canyon: the reason most people come.","source":{"label":"Team-BHP travelogue (2025)","url":"https://www.team-bhp.com/forum/travelogues/294466-ha-giang-loop-vietnam.html"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ma_Pi_Leng_Pass_winding_road_Ha_Giang_Vietnam.jpg/500px-Ma_Pi_Leng_Pass_winding_road_Ha_Giang_Vietnam.jpg","page":"Mã Pí Lèng Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ma_Pi_Leng_Pass_winding_road_Ha_Giang_Vietnam.jpg","credit":"Khánh Hmoong","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Meo Vac","place":"Meo Vac, Ha Giang","at":[23.1633,105.4104],"text":"Down from the pass to a valley town. Boats run on the river below.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Th%E1%BB%8B_tr%E1%BA%A5n_M%C3%A8o_V%E1%BA%A1c.jpg/500px-Th%E1%BB%8B_tr%E1%BA%A5n_M%C3%A8o_V%E1%BA%A1c.jpg","page":"Mèo Vạc district","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Th%E1%BB%8B_tr%E1%BA%A5n_M%C3%A8o_V%E1%BA%A1c.jpg","credit":"Khoitran1957","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Du Gia","place":"Du Gia, Ha Giang","at":[22.9312,105.2229],"text":"Rough back roads to a quiet valley of rice terraces, a waterfall 